<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketHelmet_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase") at VFEP commit e237aba (2026-08-29),
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Headgear.xml. Everything not listed under
    "Tuning" below, uiIconScale included, is still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy
    (placeholder, per TODOs.md). See Warcasket_Shipcracker.xml's header for the
    Odyssey patch findings and the WarcasketVeteran/WarcasketAll tag research;
    the same conclusion applies here.

    Tuning (2026-09-13, retuned 2026-09-17): costList ComponentSpacer 2 /
    Plasteel 60 (Siegebreaker 2 / 50). Follows the armor's 6 components / 180
    plasteel at the helmet-to-armor ratios the 10th-gen sets use: components one
    third of the armor's (Siegebreaker, Guardian and Sarcophagus 2:6, Controller
    4:12) and plasteel roughly 0.35 to 0.4 (Siegebreaker 50/145, Guardian 70/200,
    Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145; 180 x 0.35 to 0.4 is 63 to 72, rounded
    to 60, the 10th-gen helmet norm). The 09-13 pass had 3 components, a count no
    VFEP spacer helmet uses (they are 2, or 4 on Brute and Controller), which made
    this the second-priciest spacer helmet for a breathing floor and an aim buff.
    ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5, the Guardian helmet's value; see the armor's header for
    the set-wide close-combat plating rationale.

    Abilities (2026-09-16, design approved that day): the sealed helm.
    - pawnCapacityMinLevels Breathing 1.0 through VEF's ApparelExtension: a
      built-in respirator, the Sarcophagus helmet's pattern for one capacity only.
    - equippedStatFactors AimingDelayFactor x0.9: a small ranged buff so the helmet
      earns its place without Odyssey (the set's melee lean sits on the shoulders).
    - No jump-range contribution; see the armor's header.
    - Under Odyssey alone the set already totals VacuumResistance 1.0
      (0.2 + 0.1 + 0.7). Under Vanilla Gravship Expanded the compat root lowers this
      piece to 0.65 (set 0.97) and gives it VGE1's oxygen-provider comp, so the
      helmet itself restores full immunity while its oxygen lasts, no astrorig or
      pack needed; see 1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/HelmetOxygen.xml.
    - costList GravlitePanel 10 under Odyssey; see the armor's header for the split.

    SOS2/Universum parity: covered by our 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml alongside the
    armor (EVA tag + Insulation_Cold 100), mirroring what VFEP's own patch does
    for its helmets; see that file's header.
    Vanilla Gravship Expanded parity: our
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml lowers the 0.7
    below to 0.65 when VGE1 is active, the value VGE1 gives every VFEP spacer
    warcasket helmet; see the armor's header and that patch.
    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet
    (+ _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring
    VFEP's own warcasket layout.

    Draw order (2026-09-16): no drawData override, VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase's
    offsets apply unchanged. A first pass lifted this piece's south offset over
    the pauldrons, but in game that also put it over every other set's pauldrons
    at the foundry. The ordering now lives on the shoulders def (its header has
    the altitude derivation), which lowers our pauldrons under every helmet
    instead; this helmet stays interchangeable with VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase">
    <defName>SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket helmet</label>
    <shortDescription>Placeholder shipcracker warcasket helmet. Stats are an untuned copy of the siegebreaker warcasket helmet for now.</shortDescription>
    <description>Placeholder description for the shipcracker warcasket helmet. It is a stand-in for later tuning, not lore.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>1.25</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>8</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>5</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>2</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.1</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.7</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">10</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>FullHead</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerHelmet</wornGraphicPath>
      <layers>
        <li>Overhead</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <!-- priority: makes this entry the survivor when VEF merges it with the one
             VFEP_WarcasketHelmetBase carries; see the armor def's header. -->
        <priority>1</priority>
        <equippedStatFactors>
          <AimingDelayFactor>0.9</AimingDelayFactor>
        </equippedStatFactors>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Breathing</capacity>
            <minLevel>1</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
